{"id":"chatcmpl-bf882c3a-8c8b-4dda-8a67-bb066ecf44a5","object":"chat.completion","created":1795252012,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task demonstrates a multi-tool verification strategy for spatial/laterality questions in medical imaging. The key insight is to combine domain-expert interpretation, grounded coordinate reports, and targeted region-of-interest zooming to confirm directional findings before answering. The pattern generalizes to any task requiring laterality or spatial orientation confirmation from images.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When a question hinges on spatial direction (left/right, above/below), query a domain expert for a verbal description of the relevant structure's orientation before committing to an answer.\",\n    \"Use grounded reports with coordinates to independently corroborate a directional claim, since coordinates provide objective spatial evidence that complements subjective interpretation.\",\n    \"Apply region-of-interest cropping and zoom to the specific anatomical or spatial area in question to visually verify the finding rather than relying on full-image inspection.\",\n    \"Triangulate across multiple independent evidence sources (expert description, grounded coordinates, zoomed visual) before selecting a laterality-sensitive answer, since left/right errors are common failure modes.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging interpretation\": \"For laterality questions, always confirm direction via at least two independent methods (expert description + visual zoom) before answering.\",\n    \"Spatial/laterality disambiguation\": \"Convert ambiguous directional questions into explicit 'convex to which side' or 'located on which side' sub-queries to force a definitive orientation.\",\n    \"Multi-tool evidence fusion\": \"Sequence tools from coarse (expert report) to fine (ROI zoom) to progressively narrow and confirm the finding.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm the direction of the finding (e.g., convexity, displacement) is stated explicitly relative to patient anatomy, not image orientation.\",\n    \"Verify that at least two independent evidence sources agree on the laterality before finalizing the answer.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":493,"total_tokens":885,"completion_tokens":392,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":493},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":392}}}